{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already","id":456921,"title":"Stuff that's been clarified already","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-25T09:09:02-07:00","id":456921,"title":"Stuff that's been clarified already","content":"I find forums generally hard to parse through to find the information you need. As such, I wanted to make a summary thread for clarifications we've seen from writers or developers about confusing stuff from 2E that's already been clarified:<br /> <br /> After character creation, getting a new dot of your Auspice Renown grants a new Facet of both your Moon Gift and also a Shadow or Wolf Gift.<br /> <br /> New Wolf Gift Facets, on their own, cost 1XP.<br /> <br /> For Kuruth, every character has One Specific Trigger, One Common Trigger, and One Passive Trigger. <br /> The intent is that the three triggers be thematized as per the lists in the book. At least one writer uses house-rules that state that the three triggers need not have anything to do with each other. Discuss this with your group.<br /> <br /> When engaging in Social Maneuvering with a Spirit, gathra (gifts, promises, or offerings) must be given before any actions can be taken. This is both because the spirit probably starts at a hostile impression (wherein mechanically no progress can be made) and because of the laws of spirit nature dictate it to be so (in-world flavor demands that there must be an exchange, so there).<br /> <br /> <br /> Feel free to chime in with things you've had trouble with, but that people have helped you understand. Keep it short and to the point if you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":".  Changed the thing Charlaquin quoted and said was wrong 03-26-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T09:50:22-07:00","id":457004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already#post456921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Kuruth, every character has One Specific Trigger, One Common Trigger, and One Passive Trigger. The three triggers need not have anything to do with each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where was this clarified? As I recall, Chris (Acrozatarim) said that it worked that way at one time in development, and that he prefers to run it that way in his games, but that as written in the final version you pick a single category (like the moon, the other, wounds, etc) and depending on your Harmony you get the various triggers all from that same list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T10:37:25-07:00","id":457047,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Stew clarified that how it is *supposed* to work is that you choose one category and get all the triggers from that, but that my preferred way (pick each trigger freely) is an easy house rule to use if you prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T12:13:33-07:00","id":457127,"title":"","content":"Will there be a WtF 2e FAQ similar to the one for VtR 2e? After reading the extensive inquiries in the errata and other threads, it would certainly be helpful","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:23:28-07:00","id":457252,"title":"","content":"So you get 2 Facets every time you bump your Auspice renown? Yikes!<br /> <br /> --- Reflexive actions are not limited by anything short of essence expenditure<br /> <br /> --- Fighting Styles, if ST feels appropriate, are fully usable in Gauru form<br /> <br /> --- The armor listed on the character sheet for Gauru form is a typo (none of the forms have natural armor anymore)<br /> <br /> --- Father's Form does not have a duration. It is alll Gauru, all the time (until you hit, or are hit by something...then the clock starts)<br /> <br /> --- All werewolves can deal aggravated with a bite by eating their prey, even against other werewolves<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While we're on the topic, how many times can a werewolf change shape per turn? If it is reflexive, can it be done multiple times? Can it be done during other character's turns? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5304-kaimuund","name":"Kaimuund","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T13:25:49-07:00","id":457254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457252#post457252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">--- All werewolves can deal aggravated with a bite by eating their prey, even against other werewolves</div> </div> </div> </div>So far this seems to be only against humans and werewolves. It's only when you bite them in order to eat them for Essence. But not everything offers Essence to eat.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:16:47-07:00","id":457349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457254#post457254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So far this seems to be only against humans and werewolves. It's only when you bite them in order to eat them for Essence. But not everything offers Essence to eat.</div> </div> </div> </div>up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:50:24-07:00","id":457373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kaimuund</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457252#post457252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the topic, how many times can a werewolf change shape per turn? If it is reflexive, can it be done multiple times? Can it be done during other character's turns?</div> </div> </div> </div>No limit, except that you can only take one instant action per turn and if it costs you Essence your usual Essence per Turn limits. But a Harmony 4, 5, or 6 werewolf could theoretically shift as many times as they wanted in one turn. And as with all Reflexive actions, it can be done on other characters' turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T15:56:55-07:00","id":457391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already#post456921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After character creation, getting a new dot of your Auspice Renown grants a new Facet of both your Moon Gift and also a Shadow or Wolf Gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can any one point me to a post where a writer clarifies this? I see a mod saying it but not a writer. Not that I disagree with it or anything but I'd like a little bit of proof to bring to an ST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T16:59:15-07:00","id":457443,"title":"","content":"It was Chris who originally confirmed it, but I'll see if I can find the post again.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/429582-auspice-renown-and-facets?p=432036#post432036\">Here it is</a>. The thread also has some interesting discussion on the subject of starting Renown and Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-25-2015, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T17:37:41-07:00","id":457509,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3301-the-inevitable","name":"The Inevitable","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-25T19:41:33-07:00","id":457637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457047#post457047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Stew clarified that how it is *supposed* to work is that you choose one category and get all the triggers from that, but that my preferred way (pick each trigger freely) is an easy house rule to use if you prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Stew's clarification never came up in my previous big conversation about this, just yours. And as you're a writer, I took it as good enough. <br /> As written I saw no mention that you speicifically get one of each type regardless of what list you pick from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 03-25-2015, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:02:02-07:00","id":471653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=457047#post457047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Stew clarified that how it is *supposed* to work is that you choose one category and get all the triggers from that, but that my preferred way (pick each trigger freely) is an easy house rule to use if you prefer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chris, where did Stew say that? I haven't found anything here or in my email archive, and Stew's clarification seems to contradict what's pretty clearly written in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T14:22:47-07:00","id":471682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=471653#post471653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chris, where did Stew say that? I haven't found anything here or in my email archive, and Stew's clarification seems to contradict what's pretty clearly written in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think its at all clear. It says,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him. Which trigger affects him at any given time depends on his Harmony. A player should note down her character\u2019s passive, common, and specific triggers, so she knows what will affect her character when his Harmony changes. Were- wolves also have general triggers, events that will push any werewolf into Death Rage. All of the general triggers affect every werewolf; players can\u2019t pick and choose from them.&quot; </div> </div> </div>To me, this reads like you pick one set of Kuruth triggers (so, &quot;moon&quot; is one set, &quot;blood&quot; is another, &quot;wounds&quot; is another, etc.) and which trigger from that set affects you at any given time depends on your Harmony. I suppose it doesn't say you can't assemble that set from any three triggers you like, but then why are they organized into those categories in the first place, and why doesn't the text specify how many of each type of trigger I'm supposed to chose?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:28:20-07:00","id":471739,"title":"","content":"When it says, 'Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers,' to me it seems it's just referring to the personal set of theirs. And, 'A player should note down her character's passive, common, and specific triggers,' seems unnecessarily verbose if you're just grabbing a set of 'Moon triggers,' or 'The Other triggers.' In addition at the end, 'All of the general triggers affect every werewolf; players can't pick and choose from them,' implies there's more picking and choosing than, again, 'Moon triggers,' or 'Other triggers,' and so forth.<br /> <br /> So we can all agree it's unclear, at least. Of course that's why errata was being collected and why Stew was fixing things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T15:31:29-07:00","id":471743,"title":"","content":"I think the fact that we're still arguing about it is evidence enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T17:43:17-07:00","id":471906,"title":"","content":"I would have liked seeing something along the lines of &quot;the default rule is to take all the triggers under one list, but with the Storyteller's permission players may pick and choose different triggers from different lists.&quot; added. One sentence fix that clarifies everything. No need for a layout breaking sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":".  I can't avoid typos today, dammit. 04-07-2015, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T05:57:57-07:00","id":472603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=471682#post471682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, this reads like you pick one set of Kuruth triggers (so, &quot;moon&quot; is one set, &quot;blood&quot; is another, &quot;wounds&quot; is another, etc.) and which trigger from that set affects you at any given time depends on your Harmony. I suppose it doesn't say you can't assemble that set from any three triggers you like, but then why are they organized into those categories in the first place, and why doesn't the text specify how many of each type of trigger I'm supposed to chose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Funny - rereading it now, with your explanation, I can see the confusion. Before, for some reason, my brain only parsed it one way.<br /> <br /> The way I've play tested it, you pick each of your passive, common and specific triggers from any group. They don't have to mesh, or follow a theme beyond 'werewolf'. It's all part of the fun of being an imperfect-unstable-form-physical-spirit-hybrid - sometimes shit's just strange.<br /> <br /> I look at it like allergies. My uncle is allergic to shell fish and peanuts. They're very different things, but they'll get the same reaction from him (ie, possible death) if he's incautious enough to eat them. Similarly, another of my friends is allergic to cashews. Peanuts are safe for him to eat, but cashews will give him the same reaction my uncle has from peanuts.<br /> <br /> As for why they're organised under those categories in the first place, my recollection is that (1) they're werewolf-y themes, so people can be thematic if they want, and (2) it provides non-exclusive examples under each theme, so players are encouraged to make their own using these as guidelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=471906#post471906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have liked seeing something along the lines of &quot;the default rule is to take all the triggers under one list, but with the Storyteller's permission players may pick and choose different triggers from different lists.&quot; added. One sentence fix that clarifies everything. No need for a layout breaking sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this the less interesting option. If this were the case, you might as well change the first sentence of paragraph 5 in Triggers from 'Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him' to 'Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him and one-sixth of the total werewolf population, because we're making you choose one of six clearly defined lists.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I (now) acknowledge the unclear wording. Neither option will unbalance a game, so groups should do what they like. For my use, I'll be letting players actually have 'Kuruth triggers that apply just to him' by letting them mix, match, and create their own.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 04-08-2015, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:32:02-07:00","id":472630,"title":"","content":"To be honest I like that version better too. I was just reporting what I thought was the official line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:59:22-07:00","id":472882,"title":"","content":"The allergies analogy doesn't hold up fo me because I don't ever stop being allergic to cats or start being allergic to peanuts. I figured the &quot;each werewolf has a set that applies only to them&quot; was an indication that you could create your own set - not by taking triggers a la carte, but by saying &quot;I want my character to be triggered by having my authority challenged.&quot; and picking three on-theme triggers like, &quot;a packmate calls your authority into question&quot; for passive, &quot;a packmate directly challenges your ability to lead&quot; for common, and &quot;a packmate commits an act of mutiny against you&quot; for specific, or something to that effect. I guess I just took it as a given that, like with Blood, Bone, Touchstones, Breaking Points, etc. that the lists were just examples and you were free to create your own. I assumed the reason the Triggers sidebar went into what constitutes a passive, common, or specific trigger was so you'd have guidelines to construct custom trigger sets of you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:07:37-07:00","id":472888,"title":"","content":"My main issue with the Kuruth Triggers when reading it the first (few) time(s) is that it didn't seem to specifically say in the book how many of each trigger you should take. The character sheet gives two lines for each thing, but I didn't see anything else that limited the scope of personal triggers. During the initial round of debating, some people were suggesting that as your Harmony gets more out of balance you should take a whole extra set-o-three. That would play out as having just general at perfect Harmony, 1 specific at okay Harmony, 2 each of specific and common at bad Harmony, and 3 each of specific, common and passive at extremely bad Harmony.<br /> <br /> As much as I'm pro it being up to the group which set of three triggers you pick for your character (one theme is great for being thematic, all different is great for being actually unique and handwaving the &quot;supernatural stuff is weird&quot; bit; the developers seem to say the former is supposed to be cannon and the latter a house-rule), I think it has been well clarified that you should pick one of each kind of trigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:16:09-07:00","id":472893,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve been startled by realizing that when I\u2019m presented with a trigger list, I have a tendency to read it from the bottom-up, and to process it from specific up to passive rather than the reverse. When I was writing my werewolf\u2019s triggers, the specific one was the first I came up with, and then I broadened it; this led to a cohesive list, even though someone could look at it and say I picked from \u2018different lists\u2019, by a strict reading.<br /> <br /> My wolf\u2019s triggers:<br /> Specific: a werewolf pissing on her territory (or a packmate, without their consent).<br /> Common: Someone challenging her capacity to protect her territory or pack.<br /> Passive: Her pack or territory coming to harm.<br /> <br /> I mean, broadly, you could categorize as 'Pack or Territory', but the underlying theme is something harder to pin. One's an insult, the other's questioning her abilities, the last is...harm. Yet I still feel there's a logic to the progression that wouldn't be there if the passive was, for example, &quot;touching silver&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:34:04-07:00","id":472916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=472893#post472893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My wolf\u2019s triggers:<br /> Specific: a werewolf pissing on her territory (or a packmate, without their consent).<br /> Common: Someone challenging her capacity to protect her territory or pack.<br /> Passive: Her pack or territory coming to harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like your approach of starting specific and broadening out. That Spcific Trigger you took sounds pretty intense as written, though. Do you take it to mean that you have to first become aware that it happened, or does someone just need to do the pissing? Is the pissing a literal urine-marking or a more figurative &quot;mucking about in&quot;?<br /> I took Specific triggers to be a category of thing you could, with some ease, actively work to avoid. The blood one involves deciding to swallow if you taste human blood. A lot of the other ones involve being actively attacked by a specific kind of threat, thus you could make a point of avoiding those things or being diplomatic with them. The moon suggestion is the most passive (and thus uncontrolable) has a very specific set of circumstances attached to it, part of which is that it could only happen a few days out of any given month.<br /> How has yours been working out for you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:43:30-07:00","id":472928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=472916#post472916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like your approach of starting specific and broadening out. That Spcific Trigger you took sounds pretty intense as written, though. Do you take it to mean that you have to first become aware that it happened, or does someone just need to do the pissing? Is the pissing a literal urine-marking or a more figurative &quot;mucking about in&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant literal urination (hence the clarification about packmates). I'll note that my wolf's personal declared territory (she has no pack, but does have the Hunting Ground rite; this is a chat venue which just opened up, so the PCs aren't all one pack) is a large farm owned by a mostly-mortal mystery cult (I've been debating tossing the write-up for them up for public use in other games) that she's a member of; once other players come together and pack up, it'll be a larger space. And a werewolf who isn't pack urinating on that area, marking their territory, would be a grave insult to her. But I'm assuming it's when she sees/smells the piss that she'd floof into Wasu-Im.<br /> <br /> I'll report on how that goes once play gets going. We've only soft-opened thusfar, but I'm majorly excited about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:43:40-07:00","id":472929,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the idea is supposed to be that there's little you can do to avoid a passive trigger, a common trigger is avoidable as long as you take appropriate measures, and a specific trigger is something you don't usually have to work to avoid, but an enemy could use against you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:59:55-07:00","id":473393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=472882#post472882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The allergies analogy doesn't hold up fo me because I don't ever stop being allergic to cats or start being allergic to peanuts.</div> </div> </div> </div>With treatment (medication) people can stop their sensitivity to cats etc, and people can develop new allergies, even to things like peanuts. Receiving treatment and following the requirements to keep the allergy at bay sounds like balancing Harmony to me, same for developing new allergies sounds like Harmony becoming unbalanced. <br /> <br /> But, if the analogy doesn't work for you, that's fine. It doesn't really matter whether you run Kuruth triggers as all united by a theme, or pick and choose, as long as you have a set. <br /> <br /> As for how many, I believe one of each. I vaguely recall discussion that you may have developed more as your Primal Urge increased, but that doesn't appear to be in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:44:03-07:00","id":473595,"title":"","content":"That was one of Wyrdhamster's ideas, the gaining of triggers as PU rises. There are enough drawbacks to raising PU as it stands, I wouldn't use the idea, triggering less often but for longer duration is more manageable for ST and players than what Wyrdhamster had presented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:58:19-07:00","id":473620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=472603#post472603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find this the less interesting option. If this were the case, you might as well change the first sentence of paragraph 5 in Triggers from 'Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him' to 'Each werewolf has a set of Kuruth triggers that apply just to him and one-sixth of the total werewolf population, because we're making you choose one of six clearly defined lists.' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I (now) acknowledge the unclear wording. Neither option will unbalance a game, so groups should do what they like. For my use, I'll be letting players actually have 'Kuruth triggers that apply just to him' by letting them mix, match, and create their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why you don't limit players to just the printed lists in the books, I also stated that you could mix and match with ST approval. Chris already posted a nice list of additional trigger groups and the way I read it to mean in the book was &quot;X makes my character angry, so let's come up with three triggers related to that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's an example. My character was abused as a kid so I'll base his triggers around that. First the specific trigger, witnessing harm to a child. Then the passive trigger of &quot;someone yelling at a child in anger&quot;, then a common trigger of &quot;a child crying&quot;. That would make it unique to the character and still fit the trigger requirements, all while being thematically linked. I look at the lists in the book as examples of what you can do, not the only choices there are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:56:07-07:00","id":473711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=473620#post473620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's why you don't limit players to just the printed lists in the books, I also stated that you could mix and match with ST approval. Chris already posted a nice list of additional trigger groups and the way I read it to mean in the book was &quot;X makes my character angry, so let's come up with three triggers related to that.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's an example. My character was abused as a kid so I'll base his triggers around that. First the specific trigger, witnessing harm to a child. Then the passive trigger of &quot;someone yelling at a child in anger&quot;, then a common trigger of &quot;a child crying&quot;. That would make it unique to the character and still fit the trigger requirements, all while being thematically linked. I look at the lists in the book as examples of what you can do, not the only choices there are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think all three of those sound like Common triggers. Specific triggers are supposed to be things that you don't have to take any special precautions to avoid, but that an enemy could use against you if they knew it was your Trigger. Maybe a good Specific trigger related to child abuse would be <i>causing</i> harm to a child. Witnessing harm to a child is a good Common trigger because it's something you can take precautions to avoid, but is still common enough you might encounter it accidentally. Passive Triggers are meant to be things you really can't avoid, the best you can do is hope you're in a place where you won't harm anyone or anything you care about. Hearing the voice of a child in distress would be a good example. In all three cases, I wouldn't distinguish between physical or emotional harm because I don't like the implications that either is more or less harmful than the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T22:23:24-07:00","id":473888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=473711#post473711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all three cases, I wouldn't distinguish between physical or emotional harm because I don't like the implications that either is more or less harmful than the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which could be a good opportunity to have another character with a thematically similar list but a slightly (or radically) different set of triggers. My example was a quick off the top of my head kind of thing, I can see where the triggers could be tweaked, expanded or better explained.<br /> <br /> I prefer to play characters that don't share many personality traits with myself, so even if you feel one way about something (like emotional vs physical trauma as you mentioned) your character may see things differently and be bothered by things that wouldn't faze you. Interestingly enough I find that has a benefit IRL, it helps me to put myself in other people's shoes in conflict situations and my work life has benefitted for it. It's a nice feeling when people like working with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 04-09-2015, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T06:15:29-07:00","id":474213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/456921-stuff-that-s-been-clarified-already?p=473888#post473888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly enough I find that has a benefit IRL, it helps me to put myself in other people's shoes in conflict situations and my work life has benefitted for it. It's a nice feeling when people like working with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This! Roleplaying has benefited me in similar ways. Specifically, there's been a lot I've learned about communication with people who don't think like I do, from roleplaying partners who've modeled behaviors that are of use to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently playing at Fabula Rasa in the Cold Equations venue; planning an Obrimos for Fallen London.<br /> I can also be found at <a href=\"http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkersolstice.tumblr.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2192-heu","name":"Heu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T21:26:04-07:00","id":607473,"title":"","content":"Adding to this, Stew clarified in &quot;Ask a simple question...&quot; page 3 that a werewolf's personal set of kuruth triggers only trigger once per night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}